  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The PR adds the module `camcraft_sim::machine_model`.\n- The input is plain data of the module: `MachineSpec` and `PartSpec` (parts, parent, joint kind, axis, pivot, offset, travel, spindle body, tool station).\n- `camcraft-sim` gets no edge to `camcraft-post`. The caller (#2586) maps `MachineTree` into the input.\n- `generate` makes one closed body for each part that states a number:\n  - a block for a table, a bed or a slide, sized from `travel`;\n  - a cylinder for the spindle body, sized from the spindle diameter and length;\n  - a cylinder for the tool envelope, sized from the tool station. Its kind is `BodyKind::ToolEnvelope`. It is not steel.\n- Fixed, linear and rotary heads keep their stated spindle and tool-envelope bodies. A linear head with travel also keeps its slide block.\n- `MachineModel::pose` moves the bodies along the joint chain for a set of axis values. It handles linear joints, rotary joints, a pivot and an offset.\n- Each body has `BodySource::Generated`. `BodySource::judged_on()` gives \"judged on a generated model\".\n- A part with no number gets no body and a named note in `MachineModel::notes`. No size is guessed.\n- Degenerate input refuses with the part id and the key. No path panics.\n- `docs/decisions/2584-machine-model.md` records the decisions.\n\n## Cause\n\nThis is new work, not a defect. `camcraft-sim` had no machine model. The maintainer asked for a loose model from the machine file (#2574).\n\n## Tests\n\nPins, in `crates/sim/tests/machine_model.rs`:\n\n- `vmc_bodies_at_two_axis_positions`\n- `a_linear_head_keeps_its_spindle_tool_envelope_and_travel_block`\n- `a_rotary_head_keeps_and_turns_its_spindle_and_tool_envelope`\n- `tilt_head_bodies_at_two_axis_positions`\n- `a_rotary_turns_about_its_pivot_and_a_part_sits_at_its_offset`\n- `each_body_is_closed_and_marked_generated`\n- `a_part_with_no_number_gets_no_body_and_a_named_note`\n\nPins, in `crates/sim/tests/machine_model_refusals.rs`:\n\n- `the_plain_input_generates_and_poses`\n- `travel_must_be_finite_with_max_over_min`\n- `a_joint_axis_must_be_a_finite_direction`\n- `positions_must_be_finite`\n- `spindle_and_tool_station_sizes_must_be_real_lengths`\n- `the_part_list_must_be_a_tree_with_unique_ids`\n- `a_pose_states_each_joint_one_time_with_a_finite_value`\n\nRed before the change: yes. On unchanged code the suite did not compile, because the module did not exist.\n\nMutation results: 32 mutations, one at a time. Each one made a pin red. The restored tree is green.\n\n| Guard removed or changed | Red pin |\n|---|---|\n| length finite, length more than zero, length maximum | `spindle_and_tool_station_sizes_must_be_real_lengths` |\n| position finite, position maximum | `positions_must_be_finite` |\n| axis finite, axis not zero | `a_joint_axis_must_be_a_finite_direction` |\n| travel on a fixed part, travel finite, travel zero or reversed, travel maximum | `travel_must_be_finite_with_max_over_min` |\n| no part, too many parts, blank id, repeated id, parent order | `the_part_list_must_be_a_tree_with_unique_ids` |\n| pose value finite, pose value maximum, two values, unknown part, fixed part, missing value | `a_pose_states_each_joint_one_time_with_a_finite_value` |\n| chain order of the frames | `tilt_head_bodies_at_two_axis_positions`, `a_rotary_turns_about_its_pivot_and_a_part_sits_at_its_offset` |\n| pivot, offset | `a_rotary_turns_about_its_pivot_and_a_part_sits_at_its_offset` |\n| circumscribed round face | `each_body_is_closed_and_marked_generated` |\n| stack over the spindle, stack under the table | `vmc_bodies_at_two_axis_positions`, `tilt_head_bodies_at_two_axis_positions` |\n| table needs X and Y travel, no travel gives no block | `a_part_with_no_number_gets_no_body_and_a_named_note` |\n| the words \"judged on a generated model\" | `each_body_is_closed_and_marked_generated` |\n\nGate:\n\nFinal tested head: `376a0f53161916cad358700c2a61c68c084fb2f3`.\n\n- Both moving-head pins fail with the original generator. Both pass after the final generator is restored.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: GREEN, 4/4 steps. The sim library has 192 passes. Each machine-model suite has 7 passes.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: GREEN.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main`: GREEN, 223/223 steps, 0 failed steps, 63.2 minutes.\n  - `motion heavy: *`: 34 steps, 56 tests passed. Two registered failures failed as expected.\n  - `app heavy: *`: 188 steps, 42 tests passed. One registered failure failed as expected.\n  - The remaining step is the shared release build. All three registered failures refer to #1950. No unexpected test failed.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. No `.nc` file and no `.cl` file changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- `pose` has a last check that each posed vertex is finite. The input checks ahead of it stop each non-finite value. Thus no test reaches it. It stays as a backstop.\n- The winding flip of a block face for a left-handed basis. The pinned axes give right-handed bases.\n- A slide on a skew axis (not along X, Y or Z). The code handles it, but no pin has one.\n- The mapping from `MachineTree` to `MachineSpec`. It is the work of #2586. The tilt-head pin maps `assets/machines/tilthead.mch` by hand.\n- No check uses the bodies yet. The collision of machine parts is #2586.\n- The batch tier and the release tier did not run.\n\n## Notes for the review\n\n- The type is `feat`, because the issue is an enhancement with new behaviour.\n- The PR adds no user-facing command. Thus it adds no MCP tool.\n- The PR adds no dependency.\n- The sizes are loose by design. The ratios are `SECTION_RATIO` (0.25) and `BED_RATIO` (0.1).\n- A joint `axis` is the direction in which the part itself moves. The caller reverses it for a part that moves the table. The decision file gives the reason.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2763 touches `crates/sim/src/lib.rs` for a different module line. It touches the same file, different lines. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: sim: `camcraft_sim::machine_model` generates a loose machine model (blocks and cylinders) from plain part data and poses it by axis values; each body is marked \"generated\" (#2584).\n\nFixes #2584\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
